{"activity_text": "Anticancer", "article_id": "", "assay_text": "", "assay_type": "", "comments_text": "Function: Antitumor activity against A549, HCT116 and HepG2 cancer cells.\nA4K14-citropin 1.1 is a structurally optimized derivative of citropin-1.1 derived from amphibians' skin secreta peptide Citropin, which exhibits broad biological activities. Citropin-1.1 is Amphibian defense peptide with antibiotic and antimicrobial activity. Bowie and his team found that replacement of Asp4 and Gly14 with Ala and Lys (termed A4K14-CITROPIN 1.1) resulted in a more stable α-helix than Citropin on the C-terminal section, and it led to better biologicla activities", "concentration": "", "cytotoxicity_text": "No cytotoxicity information found in the reference", "hemolytic_activity_text": "No hemolysis information or data found in the reference(s) presented in this entry", "measure_group": "", "measure_value": "", "pubmed_id": "33363118", "record_granularity": "source_table_row", "reference_text": "Front Chem. 2020 Dec 10;8:616147. doi: 10.3389/fchem.2020.616147. eCollection 2020.", "sequence_key": "DRAMP:DRAMP29006", "source_id": "DRAMP29006", "source_numeric_id": "", "source_path": "DRAMP/dramp_downloads_2026-04-02/raw/Anticancer_amps.txt", "source_record_id": "Anticancer_amps:DRAMP29006", "source_table": "Anticancer_amps.txt", "stability_text": "", "subject_name": "", "target_organism_text": "[Ref.33363118] Cancer cell lines: C4-2B (IC50 = 29.05 μM), A549 (IC50 = 14.97 μM), U87 (IC50 = 14.8 μM), MCF-7 (14.16 μM)", "title": "Design, Synthesis, and Antitumor Activities Study of Stapled A4K14-Citropin 1.1 Peptides", "unit": "", "﻿database": "DRAMP"}
